<title>MEXICO: Mexican daily port, shipping update for July 23.</title>
<headline>Mexican daily port, shipping update for July 23.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>All Mexican ports were open to major shipping on Wednesday, the Communications and Transport Ministry (SCT) said in its 1000 local/1500 GMT daily meteorological report.</p>
<p>Crude shipping port Salina Cruz was shut for smaller tourism and fishing boats amid winds at 30 knots (32 miles/57 km per hour). Shipping was not limited for crude oil tankers headed across the Pacific, it said.</p>
<p>Rains were expected in the afternoon across the country, with strong wind gusts in the Gulf of Mexico.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
